  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Half-fill a large saucepan with boiling water over high heat with a pinch of salt.\n• Add spaghetti to the boiling water and cook, until ‘al dente’, 9 minutes.\n• Reserve pasta water (1/3 cup for 2 people / 2/3 cup for 4 people).\n• Drain spaghetti. TIP: ʻAl dente’ pasta is cooked through but still slightly firm in the centre.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b338592ccb8b03ddc0f495-0e5c0af5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, halve snacking tomatoes. Roughly chop kalamata olivesand capers.\n• Heat a large frying pan over medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil.\n• Cook snacking tomatoes, stirring occasionally, until blistered, 4-5 minutes.\n• Add garlic paste and a pinch of chilli flakes (if using). Cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Add tomato sugo, olives, capers and the reserved pasta water. Simmer until slightly thickened, 1-2 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b338592ccb8b03ddc0f495-3a7699ef.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove pan from heat, then stir in baby spinach leaves and cooked spaghetti, 1-2 minutes. Season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b338592ccb8b03ddc0f495-98e97e3a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide spaghetti puttanesca between bowls.\n• Top with Parmesan cheese.\n• Tear over parsley to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-67b338592ccb8b03ddc0f495-71819806.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
